.TH SDL_GetAssertionHandler 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAssertionHandler \- Get the current assertion handler.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AssertionHandler SDL_GetAssertionHandler(void **puserdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This returns the function pointer that is called when an assertion is triggered\[char46] This is either the value last passed to
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler (),
or if no application-specified function is set, is equivalent to calling
.BR SDL_GetDefaultAssertionHandler ()\[char46]
.PP
The parameter
.BR puserdata
is a pointer to a void*, which will store the \(dquserdata\(dq pointer that was passed to
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler ()\[char46]
This value will always be NULL for the default handler\[char46] If you don\(aqt care about this data, it is safe to pass a NULL pointer to this function to ignore it\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I puserdata
pointer which is filled with the \(dquserdata\(dq pointer that was passed to
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler ()\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the
.BR SDL_AssertionHandler
that is called when an assert triggers\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetAssertionHandler (3)
